Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I see a possible solution to what I want to do is geom_subplot, but that package seems to be abandoned. What I have is a CSV consisting of latitude, longitude, and magnitudes of earthquakes over the past 2 weeks and I'd like to plot it on a map. What I have so far follows:

require(maps)

require(ggplot2)

require(ggthemes)

quake.data <- read.csv('https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/feed/v1.0/summary/all_week.csv')

quake.data <- quake.data[quake.data[,15] == 'earthquake',] # earthquakes only, wtf are ice quakes anyway?

mapWorld <- borders("world", colour="gray50", fill="gray50") # create a layer of borders

ggplot() + mapWorld + geom_point(data = quake.data, aes(x=longitude, y=latitude, colour = mag, size=mag*10)) + ggtitle('Last week quakes visualised, size of the points is the magnitude', subtitle='Source: US Geological Survey') + theme_minimal()  + theme(axis.title.x = element_blank(), axis.title.y = element_blank()) + scale_colour_gradient2(guide = guide_legend(title = "Magnitude"))

Instead of geom_point, I'd rather use geom_bar to create a bar representing the earthquake's magnitude. A solution seems to be to use geom_subplot[1], but that package is archived and the package's most recent fork doesn't build on R 3.4.2[2]. Any other vectors perhaps sort this? Many thanks in advance... -- H
